# Skill: add a CRUD resource

Goal: a model with its table, a resource controller with {% if alloy %}{{ kit_name }} pages{% else %}views{% endif %} and routes, a factory and a seeder.

1. Generate everything in one command (fields are `name:type`, `?` makes a field nullable; types: `string`, `text`,
   `integer`, `bigint`, `bool`, `float`, `date`, `datetime`, `json`, `uuid`, `<name>_id:foreign`, `file` for an upload):

   ```sh
   smeltery make:model Post title:string body:text? published:bool -mcrfs
   ```

   It creates `app/models/post.rs`, `database/migrations/m<timestamp>_create_posts_table.rs`,
{%- if alloy %}
   `app/controllers/posts.rs` (returning `alloy::render("posts/{% if react %}index{% else %}Index{% endif %}")` and the other pages),
   `resources/js/pages/posts/{% if react %}{index,create,show,edit}.tsx{% else %}{Index,Create,Show,Edit}.vue{% endif %}` (the forms use `useForm`),
   `resources/js/types/post.ts` (the record's TypeScript type),
{%- else %}
   `app/controllers/posts.rs`, `resources/views/posts/{index,create,show,edit}.mold.html`,
{%- endif %}
   `database/factories/post_factory.rs` and `database/seeders/post_seeder.rs`, and registers them (the
   `r.resource("/posts")…` {% if auth %}entries{% else %}entry{% endif %} in `routes/web.rs`, the migration, the seeder).
{%- if auth %} `index` and `show` are public; `create`,
   `store`, `edit`, `update` and `destroy` are a second `r.resource("/posts")` entry with `.middleware("auth")`.
{%- else %} All seven routes are public:
   anyone can create, edit and delete records.
{%- endif %}
2. Run the migration: `smeltery migrate`. Seed if wanted: `smeltery db:seed`.
3. Adjust the validation rules on `PostForm` in `app/controllers/posts.rs` (`#[validate(required, max = 255)]`, …).
{%- if alloy %} The
   pages show a failed rule's message under its field (`form.errors.title`).
{%- endif %} A `file` field
   has a `mimes` rule (images for a name such as `image` or `photo`, else images, PDF and office or text documents);
   add types as needed, never `html`, `svg`, `xml` or `js`, which a browser runs as a page of the app.
{%- if auth %}
4. Every signed-in user may change every record. To make the whole resource private, add `.middleware("auth")` to
   the first entry too; where records belong to a user, check `auth.id()` against the record in `edit`, `update` and
   `destroy`.
{%- endif %}
{%- if alloy %}
{{ 5 if auth else 4 }}. The list and record pages get every field of the model as props (readable in the browser): when a
   model holds something private, send a struct with the public fields instead.
{{ 6 if auth else 5 }}. Add a test in `tests/` with `TestApp`: create a record through `post_alloy("/posts", &json)` and check
   `get_alloy("/posts").assert_prop("posts.0.title", …)`.
{{ 7 if auth else 6 }}. Run `smeltery test` and `npm run types`.
{%- else %}
{{ 5 if auth else 4 }}. Add a test in `tests/` with `TestApp`: create a record through `post_form("/posts", …)` and check `/posts`.
{{ 6 if auth else 5 }}. Run `smeltery test`.
{%- endif %}
